[gd_resource type="Theme" load_steps=19 format=3]


; The bronze-and-vellum grammar: the ONE owner of this game's palette, type
; scale and surface styles (docs/SHIP_PLAN.md card P5, card D11).
;
; Every hex in this file was already on screen before this card: the deep
; green, panel, bronze, teal, cream, muted and danger the expedition and
; battle prototypes each declared for themselves, plus a small set of tints
; derived from them (a raised panel, a sunken well, a hover and an active
; fill, a bright bronze, a hairline rule and its faint form, a deep teal, a
; soft danger, a focus ring and an ink for text on a lit fill). No script
; declares a hex after this card: `scripts/ui/theme_tokens.gd` reads them
; from here, and `ThemeTokens.build()` repaints every StyleBox below from
; these same tokens -- which is why the colours written into the boxes are
; the base palette's and `information_surface_test.gd` holds the two equal.
;
; Fonts: Godot's own default font carries every role; `Fonts/fonts/mono` is a
; SystemFont naming the platform's monospace family, so stable IDs line up
; without a font asset file entering the repository.

